摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"An ASCII / kinetic-typography director for MiniMax H3, with deterministic preview and seam-checked continuation. DSH plugin + portable Agent Skill.","id":"gh:1408534265","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"ascii-h3-director","slug":"YanKaFei/ascii-h3-director","topics":["agent-skill","agent-skills","ai-video","ascii","ascii-art","cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-skill","generative-art","kinetic-typography","llm","minimax","minimax-h3","motion-graphics","nodejs","terminal-art","text-art","video-generation"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"An ASCII / kinetic-typography director for MiniMax H3, with deterministic preview and seam-checked c"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ontinuation. DSH plugin + portable Agent Skill."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# ASCII H3 Director"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Costume · Art · ASCII Cinema · ASCII H3 · 2D MV · Virtual Heroine"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"中文 · **English** · 한국어 · 日本語 · Français"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> Force one idea into a chain of characters that will not stop changing shape."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What it is"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"ASCII H3 Director is a directing tool for MiniMax H3. It compiles a free-form brief into a **transfo"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"rmation chain**, a prompt written for time rather than prose, and a quality gate that stands between"},{"id":"p7s3","text":" you and the pay button. It also ships a deterministic ASCII render engine: a 5×9 hand-authored bitm"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ap font that turns the same FilmSpec into byte-reproducible terminal frames, SVGs, PNGs, and contact"},{"id":"p7s5","text":" sheets. It is both a **DeepSeek Harness (DSH) plugin** and a portable **Agent Skill**."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## What's new in v3 (against v1)"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"v1 was a Markdown skill plus bash scripts. `generate_h3.sh` forwarded to `mmx video generate`, `cont"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"inue_from_last_frame.sh` used ffmpeg to pull the last frame of the previous clip, `make_contact_shee"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"t.sh` tiled frames through an ffmpeg filter, and every directorial rule lived as prose inside `SKILL"},{"id":"p9s4","text":".md`. It worked — but the judgement was on the model's honour, and you had to pay before you could s"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"but the judgement was on the model's honour, and you had to pay before you could see a single frame."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Capability | v1 | v3 |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Shape | Markdown + bash wrappers | 8 zero-dependency ES modules + DSH plugin + Agent Skill |\n| See"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ing the frame | Generate first, then extract with ffmpeg | Deterministic preview engine — no API key"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" required |\n| Type | None (terminal font) | Hand-authored 5×9 bitmap covering all 95 printable ASCII"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" glyphs |\n| Reproducibility | Unspecified | Seeded; two renders of one FilmSpec matched SHA-256 (mea"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"sured) |\n| Motion logic | Prose rules | 21-mechanism grammar library + a `FORM_SUCCESSORS` legality "},{"id":"p11s6","text":"table |\n| Continuation | \"preserve the previous motion\" | Continuity contract: `exit_state` → `entry"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"_state` + `checkSeam` |\n| Quality | 6 self-directed questions | 7 automated checks scored /100; no P"},{"id":"p11s8","text":"ASS, no generation |\n| Reference analysis | \"extract the motion grammar\" (manual) | `reference` subc"},{"id":"p11s9","text":"ommand: STYLE DNA and chain inferred from observations |\n| Contact sheet | ffmpeg required | Built-i"},{"id":"p11s10","text":"n PNG encoder + SVG sheets, **no ffmpeg** |\n| Delivery | Anything that reads SKILL.md | DSH Cordis p"},{"id":"p11s11","text":"lugin with host tools and a Director Console panel |\n| Docs | English | Chinese / Japanese / English"},{"id":"p11s12","text":"gin with host tools and a Director Console panel |\n| Docs | English | Chinese / Japanese / English |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"**Path A — DSH plugin**"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Once installed, the plugin registers its host tools with the session and mounts the **Director Conso"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"le** panel in the Web UI."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"**Path B — generic Agent Skill**"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The installer copies `skill/` to `~/.agents/skills/ascii-h3-director/` and prints the self-check com"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"mand. The two paths do not conflict: the plugin serves DSH, the skill serves any coding agent that r"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"ths do not conflict: the plugin serves DSH, the skill serves any coding agent that reads `SKILL.md`."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Everything below is a real, copy-pasteable transcript. No API key, no cost."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Drop `--cols/--rows` to compose in the terminal first, then raise them for the final image; point `-"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"-out` at a `.svg` to get a vector sheet."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"**The one step that costs money** (and it is gated on the quality gate):"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"With `mmx` absent, `doctor` reports it as optional rather than failing — the engine never depends on"},{"id":"p25s2","text":" `mmx` absent, `doctor` reports it as optional rather than failing — the engine never depends on it."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Command reference"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| Command | Arguments | What it does |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| `plan` | `\"<brief>\" [--seed S] [--beats N] [--json]` | Full direction plan: chain, per-beat motion"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" state, quality gate |\n| `chain` | `\"<brief>\" [--beats N] [--json]` | Just the transformation chain "},{"id":"p28s3","text":"|\n| `prompt` | `\"<brief>\" [--out FILE]` | Only the compact H3 prompt |\n| `review` | `[\"<brief>\"] [--"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"out prompt.txt] [--json]` | Run the quality gate alone; `--out` audits an existing prompt |\n| `refer"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"ence` | `<obs.json> [--json]` | Extract STYLE DNA and a reproducible chain from reference observatio"},{"id":"p28s6","text":"ns |\n| `continue` | `<exit-state.json> \"<brief>\" [--json]` | Plan a seamless sequel inheriting the p"},{"id":"p28s7","text":"revious exit state, reporting seam violations |\n| `preview` | `\"<brief>\" [--t SEC] [--cols N] [--row"},{"id":"p28s8","text":"s N]` | Print one ASCII frame to the terminal |\n| `svg` | `\"<brief>\" --t SEC --out FILE.svg` | Expor"},{"id":"p28s9","text":"t one vector frame |\n| `png` | `\"<brief>\" --t SEC --out FILE.png` | Export one raster frame via the "},{"id":"p28s10","text":"built-in encoder |\n| `strip` | `\"<brief>\" [--frames N] [--cols N] [--rows N] --out FILE.png\\|.svg` |"},{"id":"p28s11","text":" Contact sheet of N evenly spaced frames; no ffmpeg |\n| `mechanisms` | `[--json]` | Print the motion"},{"id":"p28s12","text":" grammar, grouped by tier |\n| `doctor` | — | Self-check plus a real render smoke test |\n| `help` / `"},{"id":"p28s13","text":"version` | — | Usage / version |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Common flags: `--seed --beats --duration --ratio --palette --ramp --mode --text \"WORD,WORD\" --avoid "},{"id":"p29s2","text":"\"a,b\" --allow --block`, plus `--t --cols --rows --cellW --cellH` for rendering."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Choices: `--ramp` ∈ `classic brutalist minimal operators binary data phosphor typographic`; `--palet"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"te` ∈ `brutalist-digital minimal-signal phosphor paper-terminal monolith`; `--mode` ∈ `high-impact m"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"inimal-data`; `--ratio` ∈ `21:9 16:9 9:16 4:3 1:1 adaptive`."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## The motion grammar"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"A clip is not a style; it is a **transformation chain**. Characters change function over time: text "},{"id":"p32s2","text":"becomes pattern, pattern becomes particles, particles become geometry, geometry becomes space, space"},{"id":"p32s3","text":" becomes typography again. The library holds 21 mechanisms across four tiers."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"| Tier | id | Name | Emits |"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"- **Node 18+** (`doctor` checks the major version explicitly)\n- The engine has **zero runtime depend"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"encies**: it runs without a `node_modules`, and PNGs are written by the built-in encoder\n- **ffmpeg "},{"id":"p36s3","text":"is optional**: `strip`, `preview`, `svg` and `png` never need it\n- **`mmx-cli` is optional**: `npm i"},{"id":"p36s4","text":" -g mmx-cli`, used only for paid generation"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
